  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Republic of the Marshall Islands Ridge to Reef</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will contribute to UNDP-GEF R2R objective to sustain and strengthen outer island biodiversity and livelihoods in five priority outer islands: Aur, Ebon, Likiep, Mejit and Wotho through improved management of their natural resources. IOM will be responsible for carrying out four project activities: the cultural survey, socio-economic survey, feasibility study, and livelihoods implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
